      "problem": "Express $\\frac{11x-6}{(2x-3)(4x+1)(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{11x-6}{(2x-3)(4x+1)(x-1)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2x-3$ |  | $4x+1$ |  | $x-1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{11x-6}{(2x-3)(4x+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{2x-3}+\\frac{B}{4x+1}+\\frac{C}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x-3)(4x+1)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n11x-6=A(4x+1)(x-1)+B(2x-3)(x-1)+C(2x-3)(4x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(\\frac{3}{2})-6 & =A(4(\\frac{3}{2})+1)(\\frac{3}{2}-1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)(\\frac{3}{2}-1) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)(4(\\frac{3}{2})+1) \\\\ \\frac{21}{2} & =\\frac{7}{2}A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(-\\frac{1}{4})-6 & =A(4(-\\frac{1}{4})+1)(-\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-\\frac{1}{4})-3)(-\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(-\\frac{1}{4})-3)(4(-\\frac{1}{4})+1) \\\\ -\\frac{35}{4} & =\\frac{35}{8}B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11(1)-6 & =A(4(1)+1)(1-1)+B(2(1)-3)(1-1)+C(2(1)-3)(4(1)+1) \\\\ 5 & =-5C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11x-6}{(2x-3)(4x+1)(x-1)}=\\frac{3}{2x-3}-\\frac{2}{4x+1}-\\frac{1}{x-1}.\n$$",
